  <div class="legal-page">
    <h1>About TRT Guide</h1>
    <div class="legal-meta">TRT Guide LLC &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Founded Q2 2026</div>

    <p>TRT Guide exists because most "TRT clinic comparison" sites are marketing operations dressed up as editorial products. They earn money when you sign up, which means they have a financial incentive to send you to whichever clinic pays the highest commission — not to the clinic that's actually best for you.</p>

    <p>We're trying to be different. Not perfect — just more honest than the alternative.</p>

    <h2>What we do</h2>
    <p>We evaluate online TRT clinics using a 10-point rubric and publish full reviews that include pricing tables, scoring breakdowns, cited evidence, and a clear verdict. We earn affiliate revenue when you click a link and purchase, but our scores are based on merit — a bad clinic scores poorly regardless of commission rate.</p>

    <h2>Why TRT?</h2>
    <p>Testosterone replacement therapy is one of the fastest-growing segments in men's health. Online clinics have made access dramatically easier — but the review landscape is dominated by affiliate farms with surface-level "comparisons" designed to convert, not to inform.</p>
    <p>TRT is also a real medical treatment with real risks. Men deserve more than a 300-word "review" that scores every clinic 8/10 and links to the highest-paying option.</p>

    <h2>Our values</h2>
    <div class="about-values">
      <div class="about-value">
        <h3>Same rubric, every time</h3>
        <p>Every clinic gets evaluated against the same 10 criteria. No exceptions, no special treatment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-value">
        <h3>Claims are cited</h3>
        <p>Pricing, physician credentials, and service claims are verified or linked to source material.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-value">
        <h3>Transparency about revenue</h3>
        <p>FTC disclosure on every page. We tell you how we make money before you click anything.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-value">
        <h3>Quarterly updates</h3>
        <p>Reviews expire every quarter. Quality drops get reflected in updated scores.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Who runs this</h2>
    <p>TRT Guide is operated by a small, independent team. We are not backed by any clinic, investment fund, or healthcare company. We have no financial relationships with reviewed clinics beyond affiliate revenue from purchase referrals.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions, corrections, or clinic submissions: <strong>hello@trtguide.com</strong></p>
  </div>

